### Phase 0 recorded baseline (2026-07-17)

The baseline was captured without restoring the deleted tracked
`tools/Publish.ps1` and `tools/VerifyPackage.ps1`, moving `NewTools/`, or
rebuilding `dist/`. The tracked `HEAD` versions define the old publish and
verification interfaces; the existing package artifacts record their last
output. This preserves the user's in-progress cutover changes.

#### Tool contract inventory

| Surface | Parameters and environment | Dependencies | Generated/process state | Exit behavior and callers |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Old `tools/Build.ps1` | `SourceDir=src/scripts_modinstalled`, `LuaPath=''`, `LuaMode=Auto|Luac|Lua`; no environment contract | `luac` candidates, with `lua`/`loadfile()` fallback | none | Collects all syntax failures, then throws; called by README/docs and the VS Code Build task, but not by the old publisher |
| New `Build.ps1` | `LuaCompiler`, `RequiredLuaVersion`, `LiveReload=$true`, `SourceDir=src`, `DFHackRunner`, `DwarfFortressRoot`, `ReloadOutputPath`, `EnvFile=.env.local`; reads `DFHACK_LUAC`, `DFHACK_LUA_VERSION`, `DFHACK_RUNNER`, and `DWARF_FORTRESS_ROOT` directly or through `.env.local` | `Check-LuaSyntax.ps1`, `Common.ps1`, `luac.exe`, and `dfhack-run.exe` | optional reload-output file; imports missing process variables from `.env.local`; performs `<mod-id> reload` | Throws on missing tools/metadata, syntax failure, or reload failure; targeted by the VS Code Build task and called with `-LiveReload:$false` by the new publisher |
| New `Check-LuaSyntax.ps1` | `LuaCompiler=$env:DFHACK_LUAC`, `RequiredLuaVersion=$env:DFHACK_LUA_VERSION`, `IncludeTests` | `luac.exe` or configured compiler | none | Throws on missing/wrong-version compiler and first syntax failure; called by new `Build.ps1` |
| New `Common.ps1` | no script parameters; exports `Import-EnvironmentFile`, `Get-ModInfo`, and `Resolve-DFHackRunner` | PowerShell/.NET only | may set previously absent process environment variables | Helper functions throw on invalid env entries, metadata, or runner resolution; dot-sourced by new Build and Publish |
| Old `tools/Test.ps1` | `LuaPath=''`; no environment contract | explicit/discovered `lua` interpreter | none | Throws on missing runner/interpreter or nonzero test exit; called by README, `Tests/README.md`, and active feature plans |
| New `Run-UnitTests.ps1` | remaining arguments become `LuaUnitArgs`; temporarily reads/writes `LUA_PATH` and project-neutral `DFHACK_LUA_TEST_FILES` | exact LuaUnit `3.5-1`, `lua`, `luarocks`, and package-install access when the rock is absent | installs only `.luarocks/`; temporarily replaces process test/Lua paths and restores them in `finally` | Throws after cleanup for a nonzero Lua result, without terminating a caller's PowerShell host; targeted by the modified VS Code Unit Tests task |
| Old tracked `tools/Publish.ps1` | `SourceDir=src`, `OutputDir=dist`, `PackageName=''`, `NoRootFolder`, `NoExpandedFolder`; no environment contract | PowerShell copy/archive commands and old verifier | temporary staging tree, versioned zip, and optional expanded package | Throws on PowerShell/verifier failure and removes temp data in `finally`; called by README |
| New `Publish.ps1` | `SourceDir=src`, `OutputDir=dist`, `PackageName=''`; no direct environment parameters | new Common, Build, VerifyPackage, and PowerShell archive commands | temporary staging tree, versioned flat-root zip, and expanded package | Runs Build with live reload disabled, throws on build/package/verification failure, and removes temp data in `finally`; called by README after cutover |
| Old tracked `tools/VerifyPackage.ps1` | `SourceDir=src`, mandatory `ZipPath`/`PackageRoot`, optional `ExpandedPath`, `NoRootFolder` | .NET zip APIs and PowerShell filesystem reads | opens the zip; no durable output | Throws on payload-set or SoulSearch-bootstrap mismatch; called by old Publish |
| New `VerifyPackage.ps1` | mandatory `SourceDir`, `ZipPath`, and `ExpandedPath`; `PackageRoot=''` | PowerShell SHA-256 hashing and archive commands | temporary extraction tree removed in `finally` | Throws on source-shape, manifest, or content-hash mismatch; called by new Publish and intended as a standalone entrypoint |

Repository caller audit at this baseline:

- `.vscode/tasks.json` points Build at `Tools/Build.ps1` and Unit Tests at
  `Tools/Run-UnitTests.ps1`.
- `README.md` still documents `tools/Build.ps1`, the old `LuaPath`/`LuaMode`
  parameters, `tools/Test.ps1`, and `tools/Publish.ps1`.
- `Tests/README.md` still documents `tools/Test.ps1` and the publisher boundary.
- `docs/revealed-unit-filtering.todo` still uses `tools/Test.ps1` and
  `tools/Build.ps1` as future gates.
- Inside `NewTools/`, Build calls Check/Common and Publish calls
  Build/Common/VerifyPackage.

The accepted target is the new default Build contract: syntax-check production
and test Lua, load optional `.env.local`, read the mod ID from `src/info.txt`,
and run `<mod-id> reload`. `DFHACK_RUNNER` or
`DWARF_FORTRESS_ROOT` locates the runner; `DFHACK_LUAC` selects the
compiler; `DFHACK_LUA_VERSION` optionally enforces its version.

